@*
    Shared Task action dialogs -- Edit / Complete / Close / Add Evidence.

    Paired with wwwroot/js/Shared/task-actions.js (window.gracTaskActions),
    which is the ONLY code that opens, fills or submits these. Include
    this partial once on any page that wants those actions (Task Center's
    tasks.cshtml, Task View's task-view.cshtml), load task-actions.js,
    and call window.gracTaskActions.init({...}) once during that page's
    own init.

    Moved out of tasks.cshtml unchanged (change request: Task View's own
    "Actions" menu must reuse the exact same forms/modals Task Center's
    3-dot menu opens, not a second copy) so there is one markup source
    for every page that offers these actions.

    "Add Child Task" / "New Task" is NOT here -- that already had its own
    shared dialog before this change: Partials/_task-form-dialog.cshtml +
    Shared/task-form.js (window.gracTaskForm).
*@
@*
    Task View / Edit -- ONE dialog, two modes.

    View is the read-only representation of the task; Edit modifies it;
    Complete and Close are workflow actions with their own confirmations
    below. Keeping View and Edit in one dialog rather than two screens is
    deliberate: the reader who decides to edit is looking at the fields
    they want to change, and a second window would make them find their
    place again.

    The Edit button sits top-right, next to the close control, which is
    where a reader looks after finishing the page.
*@
<dialog id="taskDetailDialog" style="border:none; border-radius:8px; padding:0; max-width:980px; width:94%; box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(15,23,42,.25);">
    @* The padding lives in CSS, not inline: edit mode needs to tighten it,
       and an inline style beats any selector. Same values as before for
       the read-only view. *@
    <div class="tdd-body">
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-start; gap:12px; margin-bottom:12px;">
            <h2 id="taskDetailTitle" style="margin:0; font-size:17px;">Task</h2>
            <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; flex:0 0 auto;">
                @* Shown in view mode only; hidden while editing, because
                   an Edit button on an edit form is a dead control. *@
                <button type="button" id="taskDetailEditBtn" class="pm-button" hidden>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-pen" aria-hidden="true"></i> Edit
                </button>
                <button type="button" id="taskDetailClose" aria-label="Close" style="background:none; border:none; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer; line-height:1;">&times;</button>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="taskDetailBody"></div>
    </div>
</dialog>

<style>
    /* Task edit form (269, carried over unchanged). Scoped to
       #taskEditForm, which exists only while the dialog is in edit mode,
       so none of this can reach the read-only view or any other form on
       the page. */

    /* WIDER ONLY WHILE EDITING.
       The form carries three columns of controls where the read-only view
       carries prose, so it needs the room -- but the View keeps the width
       it has always had. setDetailMode() toggles the class. */
    #taskDetailDialog.is-editing { max-width: 1180px; }

    /* Moved off the element's inline style so edit mode can override it —
       these are the read-only view's original values, unchanged. */
    #taskDetailDialog .tdd-body { margin: 0; padding: 20px 24px; max-height: 82vh; overflow: auto; }
    /* Tighter chrome in edit mode: the padding that frames a page of
       prose is wasted around a form. */
    #taskDetailDialog.is-editing .tdd-body { padding: 16px 20px; max-height: 88vh; }

    #taskEditForm label { display: block; min-width: 0; }

    /* Three columns. Two left the four short controls stacked over four
       rows with a hint under each, which is what produced the scrollbar. */
    #taskEditForm .tef-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 10px 14px;
        align-items: start;
    }
    #taskEditForm .tef-span2 { grid-column: span 2; }

    #taskEditForm .tef-check { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; }
    #taskEditForm .tef-check input { margin-top: 2px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    #taskEditForm .tef-check .tef-h { margin-top: 0; }

    #taskEditForm .tef-l {
        display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
        color: #475569; margin-bottom: 3px;
    }
    #taskEditForm .tef-r { color: #dc2626; font-style: normal; margin-left: 2px; }
    #taskEditForm .tef-h {
        display: block; font-size: 11px; color: #64748b; margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.3;
    }

    /* Control size is NOT reduced to make things fit -- padding and font
       size are the same as every other form in the product. The height
       came out of the column count and the spacing. */
    #taskEditForm input[type="text"],
    #taskEditForm input[type="date"],
    #taskEditForm select,
    #taskEditForm textarea {
        width: 100%; padding: 6px 8px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
        border-radius: 4px; font: inherit; font-size: 13px;
        color: #0f172a; background: #fff;
    }
    /* Sized here rather than with a rows attribute so the two textareas
       stay equal and the short-viewport rule below can shrink them. */
    #taskEditForm textarea { resize: vertical; height: 76px; }

    /* A disabled control here means a governed field the rules do not let
       this task change -- the hint underneath always says which rule. */
    #taskEditForm input:disabled,
    #taskEditForm select:disabled { background: #f1f5f9; color: #64748b; }

    /* The action row stays put, so Save and Cancel are reachable even on
       a viewport short enough that the fields above have to scroll. */
    #taskEditForm .tef-actions {
        position: sticky; bottom: 0; background: #fff;
        display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 8px;
        margin-top: 12px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    }

    /* Two columns on a narrower window, one on a small screen. Below each
       breakpoint the extra column cramps rather than helps. */
    @@media (max-width: 1100px) {
        #taskEditForm .tef-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    }
    @@media (max-width: 760px) {
        #taskEditForm .tef-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        #taskEditForm .tef-span2 { grid-column: span 1; }
    }
    /* On a short viewport the textareas give up height first -- they are
       the only controls with room to spare. */
    @@media (max-height: 800px) {
        #taskEditForm textarea { height: 58px; }
        #taskEditForm .tef-grid { gap: 8px 14px; }
    }
</style>

@*
    Complete Task — a workflow action, not a field.

    sp_task_complete enforces the BRD §12 mandatory-child gate, stamps
    completed_by / completed_dt, and emits ChildCompleted plus
    ParentEligibleForCompletion on the parent. None of that is what
    "set status = Completed" would do, which is why this is not a value
    in the Edit form's status dropdown.

    Small and confirming, per the requirement: this is a decision, not
    data entry.
*@
<dialog id="taskCompleteDialog" style="border:none; border-radius:8px; padding:0; max-width:520px; width:94%; box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(15,23,42,.25);">
    <form id="taskCompleteForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Complete task</h2>
        <p id="taskCompleteSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:#334155;"></p>
        <div id="taskCompleteGate" style="display:none; font-size:12px; border-radius:5px; padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:10px;"></div>

        @* Evidence, as part of the completion workflow.
           Shown so the completer can see what is already attached, with
           the option to add more before confirming. NOT required: no
           per-task evidence-required flag exists (evidence_required lives
           on workflow_checklist_item, not practice_task) and
           sp_task_completion_eligibility does not consult evidence, so
           blocking completion on a file would be a rule this product does
           not have. *@
        <div style="margin-bottom:10px;">
            <div style="font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:#475569; margin-bottom:4px;">Evidence</div>
            <div id="taskCompleteEvidence"></div>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; margin-top:6px;">
                <input type="file" id="taskCompleteFile" style="font-size:12px; flex:1 1 auto; min-width:0;" />
                <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="taskCompleteAttach" style="padding:3px 10px; font-size:12px;">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-paperclip" aria-hidden="true"></i> Attach
                </button>
            </div>
            <span style="display:block; font-size:11px; color:#64748b; margin-top:3px;">
                Optional. Attaching is immediate and append-only &mdash; evidence is never
                overwritten or deleted, so a newer file is added alongside the old one.
            </span>
        </div>

        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:#475569; margin-bottom:3px;">Completion remark</span>
            <textarea id="taskCompleteRemark" rows="3" maxlength="4000"
                      style="width:100%; padding:6px 8px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:4px; font:inherit; font-size:13px;"
                      placeholder="What was done? Optional, but it is what the audit trail will carry."></textarea>
        </label>
        <p id="taskCompleteMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:#b91c1c;"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-complete>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Complete task
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

@*
    Close Task — shutting a task WITHOUT completing it.

    sp_task_close carries no mandatory-child gate and writes no
    completion record. It is the "superseded / duplicated / no longer
    relevant" path, and the reason is required here because a closure
    with no completion needs one to be readable later.
*@
<dialog id="taskCloseDialog" style="border:none; border-radius:8px; padding:0; max-width:520px; width:94%; box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(15,23,42,.25);">
    <form id="taskCloseForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Close task</h2>
        <p id="taskCloseSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:#334155;"></p>
        <div id="taskCloseWarn" style="display:none; font-size:12px; border-radius:5px; padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:10px;
                                      background:#fffaf0; border:1px solid #fbd38d; color:#7b341e;"></div>
        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:#475569; margin-bottom:3px;">
                Reason<span style="color:#dc2626;">*</span>
            </span>
            <textarea id="taskCloseReason" rows="3" maxlength="1000" required
                      style="width:100%; padding:6px 8px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:4px; font:inherit; font-size:13px;"
                      placeholder="Why is this being closed without completing it?"></textarea>
        </label>
        <p id="taskCloseMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:#b91c1c;"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-close>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i> Close task
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

@*
    Add Evidence — the pre-completion path.

    Evidence often has to be attached BEFORE completion, for review or
    verification, so upload cannot live only inside Complete Task. It is
    its own small action, reachable from either page's action menu at
    any point while the task is open.

    It is not part of the Edit form either: Edit is an all-or-nothing
    transactional save of task fields, while an upload is multipart,
    immediate and append-only. A validation failure elsewhere in that form
    would roll back the fields and leave the file — so they stay separate.

    Append-only is deliberate. sp_task_attachment_add is the only writer;
    there is no delete and no replace, because evidence you can quietly
    remove is not evidence. Attaching a newer file adds it alongside, and
    both keep their own uploader and timestamp.
*@
<dialog id="taskEvidenceDialog" style="border:none; border-radius:8px; padding:0; max-width:640px; width:94%; box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(15,23,42,.25);">
    <form id="taskEvidenceForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Add evidence</h2>
        <p id="taskEvidenceSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:#334155;"></p>

        <div id="taskEvidenceExisting" style="margin-bottom:10px;"></div>

        <label style="display:block; margin-bottom:8px;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:#475569; margin-bottom:3px;">
                File<span style="color:#dc2626;">*</span>
            </span>
            <input type="file" id="taskEvidenceFile" required style="font-size:12px; width:100%;" />
        </label>
        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:#475569; margin-bottom:3px;">Description</span>
            <input type="text" id="taskEvidenceDesc" maxlength="1000"
                   style="width:100%; padding:6px 8px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:4px; font:inherit; font-size:13px;"
                   placeholder="What does this file show? Recorded on the task's activity feed." />
        </label>

        <p id="taskEvidenceMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px;"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-evidence>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-paperclip" aria-hidden="true"></i> Attach evidence
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>
